#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By using these algorithms, we will learn about several design ideas that can"
" be incorporated into custom variational algorithms, such as weights, "
"penalties, over-sampling, and under-sampling. We encourage you to experiment"
" with these concepts and share your findings with the community.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan menggunakan algoritma-algoritma ini, kita akan mempelajari beberapa "
"ide desain yang bisa dimasukkan ke dalam algoritma variasional kustom, "
"seperti bobot, penalti, over-sampling, dan under-sampling. Kami mendorongmu "
"untuk bereksperimen dengan konsep-konsep ini dan berbagi temuanmu dengan "
"komunitas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit patterns framework applies to all these algorithms - but we will "
"explicitly call out the steps only in the first example.\n"
msgstr ""
"Framework pola Qiskit berlaku untuk semua algoritma ini — tapi kita hanya "
"akan secara eksplisit menyebut langkah-langkahnya di contoh pertama saja.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Variational Quantum Eigensolver (VQE) {#variational-quantum-eigensolver-vqe}"
msgstr ""
"Variational Quantum Eigensolver (VQE) {#variational-quantum-eigensolver-vqe}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[VQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.3061) is one of the most widely used "
"variational quantum algorithms, setting up a template for other algorithms "
"to build upon.\n"
msgstr ""
"[VQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.3061) adalah salah satu algoritma kuantum "
"variasional yang paling banyak digunakan, memberikan template bagi algoritma"
" lain untuk dikembangkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A diagram showing how VQE uses the reference state and ansatz to estimate "
"a cost function, and then iterate using variational "
"parameters.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqe.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A diagram showing how VQE uses the reference state and ansatz to estimate "
"a cost function, and then iterate using variational "
"parameters.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqe.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 1: Memetakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout}"
msgstr "Tata letak teoritis {#theoretical-layout}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "VQE's layout is simple:\n"
msgstr "Tata letak VQE sangat sederhana:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare reference operators $U_R$\n"
msgstr "Siapkan operator referensi $U_R$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We start from the state $|0\\rangle$ and go to the reference state "
"$|\\rho\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mulai dari state $|0\\rangle$ dan menuju ke reference state "
"$|\\rho\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Apply the variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to create an ansatz "
"$U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"
msgstr ""
"Terapkan variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ untuk membuat ansatz "
"$U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We go from the state $|\\rho\\rangle$ to "
"$U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})|\\rho\\rangle = "
"|\\psi(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita berpindah dari state $|\\rho\\rangle$ ke "
"$U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})|\\rho\\rangle = "
"|\\psi(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bootstrap at $i=0$ if we have a similar problem (typically found via "
"classical simulation or sampling)\n"
msgstr ""
"Bootstrap di $i=0$ jika kita punya masalah serupa (biasanya ditemukan "
"melalui simulasi atau sampling klasik)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each optimizer will be bootstrapped differently, resulting in an initial set"
" of parameter vectors $\\Theta_0 := \\\\{ {\\vec\\theta_{0,j} | j \\in "
"\\mathcal{J}_\\text{opt}^0} \\\\}$ (for example, from an initial point "
"$\\vec\\theta_0$).\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap optimizer akan di-bootstrap secara berbeda, menghasilkan set awal "
"vektor parameter $\\Theta_0 := \\\\{ {\\vec\\theta_{0,j} | j \\in "
"\\mathcal{J}_\\text{opt}^0} \\\\}$ (misalnya, dari titik awal "
"$\\vec\\theta_0$).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Evaluate the cost function $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\langle "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ for all "
"prepared states on a quantum computer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Evaluasi fungsi biaya $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\langle "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ untuk "
"semua state yang disiapkan di komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use a classical optimizer to select the next set of parameters "
"$\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan optimizer klasik untuk memilih set parameter berikutnya "
"$\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat the process until convergence is reached.\n"
msgstr "Ulangi proses sampai konvergensi tercapai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a simple classical optimization loop where we evaluate the cost "
"function. Some optimizers may require multiple evaluations to calculate a "
"gradient, determine the next iteration, or assess convergence.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah loop optimisasi klasik sederhana di mana kita mengevaluasi fungsi"
" biaya. Beberapa optimizer mungkin membutuhkan beberapa evaluasi untuk "
"menghitung gradien, menentukan iterasi berikutnya, atau menilai "
"konvergensi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here's the example for the following observable:\n"
msgstr "Berikut contoh untuk observable berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_1 = 2 II - 2 XX + 3 YY - 3 ZZ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_1 = 2 II - 2 XX + 3 YY - 3 ZZ,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation {#implementation}"
msgstr "Implementasi {#implementation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-"
"algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/extracted-"
"outputs/db20526e-48d4-44eb-9d2b-6c5d2ce5777e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-"
"algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/extracted-"
"outputs/db20526e-48d4-44eb-9d2b-6c5d2ce5777e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can use this cost function to calculate optimal parameters\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita bisa menggunakan fungsi biaya ini untuk menghitung parameter optimal\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-"
"for-quantum-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi kuantum {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will select the least-busy backend, and import the necessary components "
"from `qiskit_ibm_runtime`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan memilih Backend yang paling tidak sibuk, dan mengimpor komponen "
"yang diperlukan dari `qiskit_ibm_runtime`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will transpile the circuit using the preset pass manager with "
"optimization level 3, and we will apply the corresponding layout to the "
"observable.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan men-transpile Circuit menggunakan preset pass manager dengan level"
" optimisasi 3, dan kita akan menerapkan layout yang sesuai ke observable.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit Runtime primitives {#step-3-execute-using-"
"qiskit-runtime-primitives}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 3: Eksekusi menggunakan Qiskit Runtime primitives {#step-3-execute-"
"using-qiskit-runtime-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We are now ready to run our calculation on IBM Quantum&reg; hardware. "
"Because the cost function minimization is highly iterative, we will start a "
"Runtime session. This way, we will only have to wait in a queue once. Once "
"the job begins running, each iteration with updates to parameters will run "
"immediately.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang siap menjalankan perhitungan di hardware IBM Quantum&reg;. "
"Karena minimisasi fungsi biaya bersifat sangat iteratif, kita akan memulai "
"Runtime Session. Dengan cara ini, kita hanya perlu mengantri satu kali. "
"Setelah job mulai berjalan, setiap iterasi dengan pembaruan parameter akan "
"langsung berjalan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process, return result in classical format {#step-4-post-"
"process-return-result-in-classical-format}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 4: Post-process, kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik {#step-4-post-"
"process-return-result-in-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can see that the minimization routine successfully terminated, meaning we"
" reached the default tolerance of the COBYLA classical optimizer. If we "
"require a more precise result, we can specify a smaller tolerance. This may "
"indeed be the case, since the result was several percent off compared to the"
" result obtained by the simulator above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita bisa melihat bahwa rutinitas minimisasi berhasil dihentikan, artinya "
"kita mencapai toleransi default dari optimizer klasik COBYLA. Jika kita "
"membutuhkan hasil yang lebih presisi, kita bisa menentukan toleransi yang "
"lebih kecil. Ini memang mungkin diperlukan, karena hasilnya beberapa persen "
"lebih jauh dibandingkan hasil yang diperoleh simulator di atas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The value of x obtained is the current best guess for the parameters that "
"minimize the cost function. If iterating to obtain a higher precision, those"
" values should be used in place of the x0 initially used (a vector of "
"ones).\n"
msgstr ""
"Nilai x yang diperoleh adalah tebakan terbaik saat ini untuk parameter yang "
"meminimalkan fungsi biaya. Jika melakukan iterasi untuk mendapatkan presisi "
"yang lebih tinggi, nilai-nilai tersebut harus digunakan sebagai pengganti x0"
" yang awalnya digunakan (vektor berisi angka satu).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, we note that the function was evaluated 96 times in the process of "
"optimization. That might be different from the number of optimization steps,"
" since some optimizers require multiple function evaluations in a single "
"step, such as when estimating a gradient.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terakhir, kita catat bahwa fungsi dievaluasi sebanyak 96 kali dalam proses "
"optimisasi. Jumlah ini bisa berbeda dari jumlah langkah optimisasi, karena "
"beberapa optimizer membutuhkan beberapa evaluasi fungsi dalam satu langkah, "
"misalnya saat memperkirakan gradien.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Subspace Search VQE (SSVQE) {#subspace-search-vqe-ssvqe}"
msgstr "Subspace Search VQE (SSVQE) {#subspace-search-vqe-ssvqe}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[SSVQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.09434) is a variant of VQE that allows "
"obtaining the first $k$ eigenvalues of an observable $\\hat{H}$ with "
"eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, where $N\\geq"
" k$. Without loss of generality, we assume that "
"$\\lambda_0<\\lambda_1<...<\\lambda_{N-1}$. SSVQE introduces a new idea by "
"adding weights to help prioritize optimizing for the term with the largest "
"weight.\n"
msgstr ""
"[SSVQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.09434) adalah varian dari VQE yang "
"memungkinkan mendapatkan $k$ eigenvalue pertama dari observable $\\hat{H}$ "
"dengan eigenvalue $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, di mana"
" $N\\geq k$. Tanpa kehilangan generalitas, kita asumsikan bahwa "
"$\\lambda_0<\\lambda_1<...<\\lambda_{N-1}$. SSVQE memperkenalkan ide baru "
"dengan menambahkan bobot untuk membantu memprioritaskan optimisasi untuk "
"suku dengan bobot terbesar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A diagram showing how subspace-search VQE uses the components of "
"variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/instances-and-extensions/instances-ssvqe.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A diagram showing how subspace-search VQE uses the components of "
"variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/instances-and-extensions/instances-ssvqe.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To implement this algorithm, we need $k$ mutually orthogonal reference "
"states $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, meaning $\\langle \\rho_j | "
"\\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ for $j,l<k$. These states can be "
"constructed using Pauli operators. The cost function of this algorithm is "
"then:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengimplementasikan algoritma ini, kita membutuhkan $k$ reference "
"state yang saling ortogonal $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, artinya "
"$\\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ untuk $j,l<k$. State-"
"state ini bisa dikonstruksi menggunakan operator Pauli. Fungsi biaya dari "
"algoritma ini kemudian adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{\\theta})\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{\\theta})\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\rho_j | "
"U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})\\hat{H} U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j "
"\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\rho_j | "
"U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})\\hat{H} U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j "
"\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $w_j$ is an arbitrary positive number such that if $j<l<k$ then "
"$w_j>w_l$, and $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$ is the user-defined variational form.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $w_j$ adalah bilangan positif sembarang sedemikian sehingga jika "
"$j<l<k$ maka $w_j>w_l$, dan $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$ adalah variational form "
"yang didefinisikan pengguna.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The SSVQE algorithm relies on the fact that eigenstates corresponding to "
"different eigenvalues are mutually orthogonal. Specifically, the inner "
"product of $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle$ and "
"$U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l\\rangle$ can be expressed as:\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma SSVQE bergantung pada fakta bahwa eigenstate yang bersesuaian "
"dengan eigenvalue yang berbeda saling ortogonal. Secara spesifik, hasil kali"
" dalam dari $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle$ dan "
"$U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l\\rangle$ bisa diekspresikan sebagai:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l \\rangle\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l \\rangle\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\langle \\rho_j | I |\\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\langle \\rho_j | I |\\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\delta_{jl}\n"
msgstr "& = \\delta_{jl}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first equality holds because $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})$ is a quantum "
"operator and is therefore unitary. The last equality holds because of the "
"orthogonality of the reference states $|\\rho_j\\rangle$. The fact that "
"orthogonality is preserved through unitary transformations is deeply related"
" to the principle of conservation of information, as expressed in quantum "
"information science. Under this view, non-unitary transformations represent "
"processes where information is either lost or injected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kesamaan pertama berlaku karena $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})$ adalah operator "
"kuantum dan karenanya bersifat uniter. Kesamaan terakhir berlaku karena "
"ortogonalitas reference state $|\\rho_j\\rangle$. Fakta bahwa ortogonalitas "
"dipertahankan melalui transformasi uniter berkaitan erat dengan prinsip "
"konservasi informasi, sebagaimana dinyatakan dalam ilmu informasi kuantum. "
"Dalam sudut pandang ini, transformasi non-uniter merepresentasikan proses di"
" mana informasi hilang atau disuntikkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Weights $w_j$ help ensure that all the states are eigenstates. If the "
"weights are sufficiently different, the term with the largest weight (that "
"is, $w_0$) will be given priority during optimization over the others. As a "
"result, the resulting state $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_0 \\rangle$ will "
"become the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_0$. Because $\\{ "
"U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$ are mutually "
"orthogonal, the remaining states will be orthogonal to it and, therefore, "
"contained in the subspace corresponding to the eigenvalues "
"$\\{\\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bobot $w_j$ membantu memastikan bahwa semua state adalah eigenstate. Jika "
"bobot-bobot cukup berbeda, suku dengan bobot terbesar (yaitu, $w_0$) akan "
"diprioritaskan selama optimisasi dibanding yang lain. Akibatnya, state yang "
"dihasilkan $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_0 \\rangle$ akan menjadi eigenstate "
"yang bersesuaian dengan $\\lambda_0$. Karena $\\{ "
"U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$ saling ortogonal, "
"state-state yang tersisa akan ortogonal terhadapnya dan, oleh karena itu, "
"terkandung dalam subspace yang bersesuaian dengan eigenvalue "
"$\\{\\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applying the same argument to the rest of the terms, the next priority would"
" then be the term with weight $w_1$, so $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_1 "
"\\rangle$ would be the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_1$, and the "
"other terms would be contained in the eigenspace of "
"$\\{\\lambda_2,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menerapkan argumen yang sama untuk sisa suku, prioritas berikutnya adalah "
"suku dengan bobot $w_1$, sehingga $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_1 \\rangle$ "
"akan menjadi eigenstate yang bersesuaian dengan $\\lambda_1$, dan suku "
"lainnya akan terkandung dalam eigenspace dari "
"$\\{\\lambda_2,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By reasoning inductively, we deduce that $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j "
"\\rangle$ will be an approximate eigenstate of $\\lambda_j$ for $0\\leq j < "
"k.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan penalaran induktif, kita menyimpulkan bahwa "
"$U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j \\rangle$ akan menjadi eigenstate perkiraan "
"dari $\\lambda_j$ untuk $0\\leq j < k.$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout-1}"
msgstr "Tata letak teoritis {#theoretical-layout-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "SSVQE's can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr "SSVQE dapat dirangkum sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prepare several reference states by applying a unitary U_R to k different "
"computational basis states\n"
msgstr ""
"Siapkan beberapa reference state dengan menerapkan uniter U_R ke k state "
"basis komputasi yang berbeda\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This algorithm requires the usage of $k$ mutually orthogonal reference "
"states $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, such that $\\langle \\rho_j |"
" \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ for $j,l<k$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma ini membutuhkan penggunaan $k$ reference state yang saling "
"ortogonal $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, sedemikian sehingga "
"$\\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ untuk $j,l<k$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Apply the variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to each reference "
"state, resulting in the following ansatz $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terapkan variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ ke setiap reference "
"state, menghasilkan ansatz berikut $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bootstrap at $i=0$ if a similar problem is available (usually found via "
"classical simulation or sampling).\n"
msgstr ""
"Bootstrap di $i=0$ jika masalah serupa tersedia (biasanya ditemukan melalui "
"simulasi atau sampling klasik).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Evaluate the cost function $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j "
"\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) "
"\\rangle$ for all prepared states on a quantum computer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Evaluasi fungsi biaya $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j "
"\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) "
"\\rangle$ untuk semua state yang disiapkan di komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be separated into calculating the expectation value for an "
"observable $\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ and multiplying that result by $w_j$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini bisa dipisahkan menjadi menghitung nilai ekspektasi untuk observable "
"$\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) "
"\\rangle$ dan mengalikan hasilnya dengan $w_j$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Afterward, the cost function returns the sum of all weighted expectation "
"values.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah itu, fungsi biaya mengembalikan jumlah semua nilai ekspektasi "
"berbobot.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use a classical optimizer to determine the next set of parameters "
"$\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan optimizer klasik untuk menentukan set parameter berikutnya "
"$\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat the above steps until convergence is achieved.\n"
msgstr "Ulangi langkah-langkah di atas sampai konvergensi tercapai.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You will be reconstructing SSVQE's cost function in the assessment, but we "
"have the following snippet to motivate your solution:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu akan merekonstruksi fungsi biaya SSVQE dalam penilaian, tapi kita punya"
" cuplikan berikut untuk memotivasi solusimu:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Variational Quantum Deflation (VQD) {#variational-quantum-deflation-vqd}"
msgstr ""
"Variational Quantum Deflation (VQD) {#variational-quantum-deflation-vqd}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[VQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08138) is an iterative method that extends "
"VQE to obtain the first $k$ eigenvalues of an observable $\\hat{H}$ with "
"eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, where $N\\geq"
" k$, instead of only the first. For the rest of this section, we will "
"assume, without loss of generality, that "
"$\\lambda_0\\leq\\lambda_1\\leq...\\leq\\lambda_{N-1}$. VQD introduces the "
"notion of a penalty cost to guide the optimization process.\n"
msgstr ""
"[VQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08138) adalah metode iteratif yang "
"memperluas VQE untuk mendapatkan $k$ nilai eigen pertama dari suatu "
"observable $\\hat{H}$ dengan nilai eigen $\\{\\lambda_0, "
"\\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, di mana $N\\geq k$, bukan hanya yang "
"pertama. Untuk sisa bagian ini, kita akan mengasumsikan, tanpa mengurangi "
"keumuman, bahwa $\\lambda_0\\leq\\lambda_1\\leq...\\leq\\lambda_{N-1}$. VQD "
"memperkenalkan konsep biaya penalti untuk memandu proses optimasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A diagram showing how VQD uses the components of a variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqd.svg)\n"
"VQD introduces a penalty term, denoted as $\\beta$, to balance the contribution of each overlap term to the cost. This penalty term serves to penalize the optimization process if orthogonality is not achieved. We impose this constraint because the eigenstates of an observable, or a Hermitian operator, corresponding to different eigenvalues are always mutually orthogonal, or can be made to be so in the case of degeneracy or repeated eigenvalues. Thus, by enforcing orthogonality with the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_0$, we are effectively optimizing over the subspace that corresponds to the rest of the eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2,..., \\lambda_{N-1}\\}$. Here, $\\lambda_1$ is the lowest eigenvalue from the rest of the eigenvalues and, therefore, the optimal solution of the new problem can be obtained using the variational theorem.\n"
msgstr ""
"![Diagram yang menunjukkan bagaimana VQD menggunakan komponen-komponen algoritma variasional.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-vqd.svg)\n"
"VQD memperkenalkan istilah penalti, dilambangkan sebagai $\\beta$, untuk menyeimbangkan kontribusi setiap istilah overlap terhadap biaya. Istilah penalti ini berfungsi untuk menghukum proses optimasi jika ortogonalitas tidak tercapai. Kita memberlakukan batasan ini karena eigenstate dari suatu observable, atau operator Hermitian, yang bersesuaian dengan nilai eigen yang berbeda selalu saling ortogonal, atau dapat dibuat demikian dalam kasus degenerasi atau nilai eigen yang berulang. Dengan demikian, dengan menegakkan ortogonalitas terhadap eigenstate yang bersesuaian dengan $\\lambda_0$, kita secara efektif mengoptimalkan atas subruang yang bersesuaian dengan sisa nilai eigen $\\{\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2,..., \\lambda_{N-1}\\}$. Di sini, $\\lambda_1$ adalah nilai eigen terendah dari sisa nilai eigen dan, oleh karena itu, solusi optimal dari masalah baru dapat diperoleh menggunakan teorema variasional.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The general idea behind VQD is to use VQE as usual to obtain the lowest "
"eigenvalue $\\lambda_0 := C_0(\\vec\\theta^0) \\equiv "
"C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec\\theta^0)$ along with the corresponding (approximate) "
"eigenstate $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ for some optimal parameter "
"vector $\\vec{\\theta^0}$. Then, to obtain the next eigenvalue $\\lambda_1 >"
" \\lambda_0$, instead of minimizing the cost function $C_0(\\vec{\\theta}) "
":= \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$, we optimize:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ide umum di balik VQD adalah menggunakan VQE seperti biasa untuk mendapatkan"
" nilai eigen terendah $\\lambda_0 := C_0(\\vec\\theta^0) \\equiv "
"C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec\\theta^0)$ beserta eigenstate (perkiraan) yang "
"bersesuaian $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ untuk vektor parameter "
"optimal $\\vec{\\theta^0}$. Kemudian, untuk mendapatkan nilai eigen "
"berikutnya $\\lambda_1 > \\lambda_0$, alih-alih meminimalkan fungsi biaya "
"$C_0(\\vec{\\theta}) := \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$, kita mengoptimalkan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_0(\\vec{\\theta})+ \\beta_0 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_0(\\vec{\\theta})+ \\beta_0 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The positive value $\\beta_0$ should ideally be greater than "
"$\\lambda_1-\\lambda_0$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nilai positif $\\beta_0$ idealnya harus lebih besar dari "
"$\\lambda_1-\\lambda_0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This introduces a new cost function that can be viewed as a constrained "
"problem, where we minimize $C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ subject to"
" the constraint that the state must be orthogonal to the previously obtained"
" $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$, with $\\beta_0$ acting as a penalty "
"term if the constraint is not satisfied.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini memperkenalkan fungsi biaya baru yang dapat dipandang sebagai masalah "
"terkendala, di mana kita meminimalkan $C_\\text{VQE}(\\vec{\\theta}) = "
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ "
"dengan syarat bahwa state harus ortogonal terhadap "
"$|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ yang telah diperoleh sebelumnya, dengan "
"$\\beta_0$ bertindak sebagai istilah penalti jika syarat tidak terpenuhi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively, this new problem can be interpreted as running VQE on the new"
" observable:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai alternatif, masalah baru ini dapat diinterpretasikan sebagai "
"menjalankan VQE pada observable baru:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_1} := \\hat{H} + \\beta_0 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_1} := \\hat{H} + \\beta_0 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assuming that the solution to the new problem is $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$, the expected value of $\\hat{H}$ (not $\\hat{H_1}$) should be $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle = \\lambda_1$.\n"
"To obtain the third eigenvalue $\\lambda_2$, the cost function to optimize is:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan asumsi bahwa solusi untuk masalah baru adalah $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$, nilai ekspektasi dari $\\hat{H}$ (bukan $\\hat{H_1}$) seharusnya $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle = \\lambda_1$.\n"
"Untuk mendapatkan nilai eigen ketiga $\\lambda_2$, fungsi biaya yang perlu dioptimalkan adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_1 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_1(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_1 |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\beta_1$ is a positive constant large enough to enforce "
"orthogonality of the solution state to both "
"$|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ and $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$. "
"This penalizes states in the search space that do not meet this requirement,"
" effectively restricting the search space. Thus, the optimal solution of the"
" new problem should be the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_2$.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $\\beta_1$ adalah konstanta positif yang cukup besar untuk "
"menegakkan ortogonalitas state solusi terhadap "
"$|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^0})\\rangle$ dan $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle$. "
"Ini menghukum state dalam ruang pencarian yang tidak memenuhi persyaratan "
"ini, sehingga secara efektif membatasi ruang pencarian. Dengan demikian, "
"solusi optimal dari masalah baru seharusnya adalah eigenstate yang "
"bersesuaian dengan $\\lambda_2$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Like the previous case, this new problem can also be interpreted as VQE with"
" the observable:\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti kasus sebelumnya, masalah baru ini juga dapat diinterpretasikan "
"sebagai VQE dengan observable:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_2} := \\hat{H_1} + \\beta_1 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_2} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H_2} := \\hat{H_1} + \\beta_1 |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^1})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_2(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H_2} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the solution to this new problem is $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle$, the expected value of $\\hat{H}$ (not $\\hat{H_2}$) should be $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle = \\lambda_2$.\n"
"Analogously, to obtain the $k$-th eigenvalue $\\lambda_{k-1}$, you would minimize the cost function:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika solusi untuk masalah baru ini adalah $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle$, nilai ekspektasi dari $\\hat{H}$ (bukan $\\hat{H_2}$) seharusnya $ \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^2})\\rangle = \\lambda_2$.\n"
"Secara analog, untuk mendapatkan nilai eigen ke-$k$ yaitu $\\lambda_{k-1}$, kamu perlu meminimalkan fungsi biaya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_{k-2}(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_{k-2} |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle  |^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"C_{k-2}(\\vec{\\theta}) + \\beta_{k-2} |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle  |^2,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Remember that we defined $\\vec{\\theta^j}$ such that $\\langle "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle = "
"\\lambda_j, \\forall j<k$. This problem is equivalent to minimizing "
"$C(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ but with the constraint that the state must "
"be orthogonal to $|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle ; \\forall j \\in {0, "
"\\cdots, k-1}$, thereby restricting the search space to the subspace "
"corresponding to the eigenvalues "
"$\\{\\lambda_{k-1},\\cdots,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahwa kita mendefinisikan $\\vec{\\theta^j}$ sedemikian sehingga "
"$\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) | \\hat{H} | "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle = \\lambda_j, \\forall j<k$. Masalah ini "
"setara dengan meminimalkan $C(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ tetapi "
"dengan syarat bahwa state harus ortogonal terhadap "
"$|\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle ; \\forall j \\in {0, \\cdots, k-1}$, "
"sehingga membatasi ruang pencarian ke subruang yang bersesuaian dengan nilai"
" eigen $\\{\\lambda_{k-1},\\cdots,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This problem is equivalent to a VQE with the observable:\n"
msgstr "Masalah ini setara dengan VQE dengan observable:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-1} :=\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-2} + \\beta_{k-2} |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H}_{k-1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-1} :=\n"
"\\hat{H}_{k-2} + \\beta_{k-2} |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})\\rangle \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^{k-2}})|\n"
"\\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad\n"
"C_{k-1}(\\vec{\\theta}) = \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H}_{k-1} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As you can see from the process, to obtain the $k$-th eigenvalue, you need "
"the (approximate) eigenstates of the previous $k-1$ eigenvalues, so you "
"would need to run VQE a total of $k$ times. Therefore, VQD's cost function "
"is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang bisa kamu lihat dari prosesnya, untuk mendapatkan nilai eigen "
"ke-$k$, kamu membutuhkan eigenstate (perkiraan) dari $k-1$ nilai eigen "
"sebelumnya, sehingga kamu perlu menjalankan VQE sebanyak $k$ kali. Oleh "
"karena itu, fungsi biaya VQD adalah sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_k(\\vec{\\theta}) =\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_k(\\vec{\\theta}) =\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout-2}"
msgstr "Tata letak teoritis {#theoretical-layout-2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "VQD's layout can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr "Tata letak VQD dapat dirangkum sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare a reference operator $U_R$\n"
msgstr "Siapkan operator referensi $U_R$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Apply variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to the reference state, "
"creating the following ansatze $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"
msgstr ""
"Terapkan variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ pada state referensi, "
"membuat ansatz berikut $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bootstrap at $i=0$ if we have a similar problem (typically found via "
"classical simulation or sampling).\n"
msgstr ""
"Bootstrap pada $i=0$ jika kita punya masalah serupa (biasanya ditemukan via "
"simulasi atau sampling klasik).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Evaluate the cost function $C_k(\\vec{\\theta})$, which involves computing "
"$k$ excited states and an array of $\\beta$'s defining the overlap penalty "
"for each overlap term.\n"
msgstr ""
"Evaluasi fungsi biaya $C_k(\\vec{\\theta})$, yang melibatkan komputasi $k$ "
"excited state dan array $\\beta$ yang mendefinisikan penalti overlap untuk "
"setiap istilah overlap.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calculate the expectation value for an observable $\\langle "
"\\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ "
"for each $k$\n"
msgstr ""
"Hitung nilai ekspektasi untuk observable $\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta})"
" | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ untuk setiap $k$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calculate the penalty $\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hitung penalti $\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| "
"\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle |^2$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The cost function should then return the sum of these two terms\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi biaya kemudian harus mengembalikan jumlah dari kedua istilah ini\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use a classical optimizer to choose the next set of parameters "
"$\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan pengoptimal klasik untuk memilih set parameter berikutnya "
"$\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat this process until convergence is reached.\n"
msgstr "Ulangi proses ini hingga konvergensi tercapai.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation {#implementation-1}"
msgstr "Implementasi {#implementation-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this implementation, we'll create a function for an overlap penalty. "
"This penalty will be used in the cost function at each iteration. This "
"process will be repeated for each excited state\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk implementasi ini, kita akan membuat fungsi untuk penalti overlap. "
"Penalti ini akan digunakan dalam fungsi biaya di setiap iterasi. Proses ini "
"akan diulang untuk setiap excited state\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-"
"algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/extracted-"
"outputs/9d368de5-d512-4fe8-8842-9c735944b22b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output dari sel kode sebelumnya](/learning/images/courses/variational-"
"algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/extracted-"
"outputs/9d368de5-d512-4fe8-8842-9c735944b22b-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, we'll set up a function that calculates the state fidelity -- a "
"percentage of overlap between two states that we'll use as a penalty for "
"VQD:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, kita akan menyiapkan fungsi yang menghitung fidelitas state -- "
"persentase overlap antara dua state yang akan kita gunakan sebagai penalti "
"untuk VQD:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's time to write VQD's cost function. As before when we calculated only "
"the ground state, we will determine the lowest energy state using the "
"Estimator primitive. However, as described above, we will now add a penalty "
"term to ensure orthogonality of higher-energy states. That is, for each new "
"excited state, a penalty is added for any overlap between the current "
"variational state and the lower-energy eigenstates already found.\n"
msgstr ""
"Saatnya menulis fungsi biaya VQD. Seperti sebelumnya ketika kita hanya "
"menghitung ground state, kita akan menentukan state energi terendah "
"menggunakan primitif Estimator. Namun, seperti yang dijelaskan di atas, kita"
" sekarang akan menambahkan istilah penalti untuk memastikan ortogonalitas "
"state berenergi lebih tinggi. Artinya, untuk setiap excited state baru, "
"penalti ditambahkan untuk setiap overlap antara state variasional saat ini "
"dan eigenstate berenergi lebih rendah yang sudah ditemukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note especially that the cost function above refers to the "
"`calculate_overlaps` function, which actually creates a new quantum circuit."
" If we want to run on real hardware, that new circuit must also be "
"transpiled, hopefully in an optimal way, to run on the backend we select. "
"Note that transpilation has been built in to the `calculate_overlaps` or "
"`cost_func_vqd` functions. Feel free to try modifying the code yourself to "
"build in this additional (and conditional) transpilation - but this will "
"also be done for you in the next lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan terutama bahwa fungsi biaya di atas merujuk ke fungsi "
"`calculate_overlaps`, yang sebenarnya membuat Circuit quantum baru. Jika "
"kita ingin menjalankan pada hardware nyata, Circuit baru tersebut juga harus"
" ditranspilasi, sebaiknya dengan cara yang optimal, untuk dijalankan pada "
"Backend yang kita pilih. Perhatikan bahwa transpilasi telah dibangun ke "
"dalam fungsi `calculate_overlaps` atau `cost_func_vqd`. Silakan coba "
"modifikasi kode sendiri untuk membangun transpilasi tambahan (dan "
"kondisional) ini — tapi ini juga akan dilakukan untukmu di pelajaran "
"berikutnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we will run the VQD algorithm using the Statevector Sampler "
"and Statevector Estimator:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran ini, kita akan menjalankan algoritma VQD menggunakan "
"Statevector Sampler dan Statevector Estimator:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will introduce an observable to be estimated. In the next lesson we will "
"add some physical context to this, like the excited state of a molecule. It "
"may be helpful to think of this observable as the Hamiltonian of a system "
"that can have excited states, even though this observable has not been "
"chosen to match any particular molecule or atom.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan memperkenalkan observable yang akan diestimasi. Di pelajaran "
"berikutnya kita akan menambahkan beberapa konteks fisik pada ini, seperti "
"excited state dari suatu molekul. Mungkin membantu untuk memikirkan "
"observable ini sebagai Hamiltonian dari sistem yang dapat memiliki excited "
"state, meskipun observable ini tidak dipilih untuk cocok dengan molekul atau"
" atom tertentu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we set the total number of states we wish to calculate (ground state "
"and excited states, k), and the penalties (betas) for overlap between "
"statevectors that should be orthogonal. The consequences of choosing betas "
"to be too high or too low will be explored a bit in the next lesson. For "
"now, we will simply use those provided below. We will start by using all "
"zeros as our parameters. In your own calculations, you may want to use more "
"clever starting parameters based on your knowledge of the system or on "
"previous calculations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita menetapkan jumlah total state yang ingin kita hitung (ground "
"state dan excited state, k), dan penalti (betas) untuk overlap antara "
"statevector yang seharusnya ortogonal. Konsekuensi dari memilih betas "
"terlalu tinggi atau terlalu rendah akan dieksplorasi sedikit di pelajaran "
"berikutnya. Untuk sekarang, kita akan menggunakan yang disediakan di bawah. "
"Kita akan mulai dengan menggunakan semua nol sebagai parameter kita. Dalam "
"perhitunganmu sendiri, kamu mungkin ingin menggunakan parameter awal yang "
"lebih cerdas berdasarkan pengetahuanmu tentang sistem atau berdasarkan "
"perhitungan sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can now run the calculation:\n"
msgstr "Kita sekarang dapat menjalankan perhitungan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The values we obtained from the cost function are approximately -6.00, 4.02,"
" and 5.61. The important thing about these results is that the function "
"values are increasing. If we had obtained a first excited state that is "
"lower in energy than our initial, unconstrained calculation of the ground "
"state, that would have indicated an error somewhere in our code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nilai yang kita peroleh dari fungsi biaya adalah sekitar -6.00, 4.02, dan "
"5.61. Hal penting tentang hasil ini adalah bahwa nilai fungsinya meningkat. "
"Jika kita mendapatkan excited state pertama yang energinya lebih rendah dari"
" perhitungan awal ground state tanpa kendala, itu akan menunjukkan adanya "
"kesalahan di suatu tempat dalam kode kita.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The values of x are the parameters that yielded a statevector corresponding "
"to each of these costs (energies).\n"
msgstr ""
"Nilai x adalah parameter yang menghasilkan statevector yang bersesuaian "
"dengan masing-masing biaya (energi) ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, we note that all three minimizations converged to within the "
"default tolerance of the classical optimizer (here COBYLA). They required "
"131, 110, and 90 function evaluations, respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terakhir, kita mencatat bahwa ketiga minimisasi berkonvergensi dalam "
"toleransi default pengoptimal klasik (di sini COBYLA). Masing-masing "
"memerlukan 131, 110, dan 90 evaluasi fungsi.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum Sampling Regression (QSR) {#quantum-sampling-regression-qsr}"
msgstr "Quantum Sampling Regression (QSR) {#quantum-sampling-regression-qsr}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One of the main issues with VQE is the multiple calls to a quantum computer "
"that are required to obtain the parameters for each step, for example, $k$, "
"$k-1$, and so on. This is especially problematic when access to quantum "
"devices is queued. While a [`Session`](/guides/run-jobs-session) can be used"
" to group multiple iterative calls, an alternative approach is to use "
"sampling. By utilizing more classical resources, we can complete the full "
"optimization process in a single call. This is where [Quantum Sampling "
"Regression](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.02338) comes into play. Since access "
"to quantum computers is still a low-offer/high-demand commodity, we find "
"this trade-off to be both possible and convenient for many current studies. "
"This approach harnesses all available classical capabilities while still "
"capturing many of the inner workings and intrinsic properties of quantum "
"computations that do not appear in simulation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Salah satu masalah utama dengan VQE adalah banyaknya panggilan ke komputer "
"kuantum yang diperlukan untuk mendapatkan parameter di setiap langkah, "
"misalnya, $k$, $k-1$, dan seterusnya. Ini sangat bermasalah ketika akses ke "
"perangkat kuantum harus mengantri. Meskipun [`Session`](/guides/run-jobs-"
"session) dapat digunakan untuk mengelompokkan beberapa panggilan iteratif, "
"pendekatan alternatif adalah menggunakan sampling. Dengan memanfaatkan lebih"
" banyak sumber daya klasik, kita dapat menyelesaikan seluruh proses optimasi"
" dalam satu panggilan. Di sinilah [Quantum Sampling "
"Regression](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.02338) berperan. Karena akses ke "
"komputer kuantum masih merupakan komoditas rendah penawaran/tinggi "
"permintaan, kita menemukan trade-off ini menjadi mungkin dan nyaman untuk "
"banyak studi saat ini. Pendekatan ini memanfaatkan semua kemampuan klasik "
"yang tersedia sambil tetap menangkap banyak cara kerja internal dan sifat "
"intrinsik komputasi kuantum yang tidak muncul dalam simulasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A diagram showing how QSR uses the components of a variational "
"algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-"
"and-extensions/instances-qsr.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Diagram yang menunjukkan bagaimana QSR menggunakan komponen-komponen "
"algoritma variasional.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-"
"design/instances-and-extensions/instances-qsr.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The idea behind QSR is that the cost function $C(\\theta) := \\langle "
"\\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle$ can be expressed as a "
"Fourier series in the following manner:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ide di balik QSR adalah bahwa fungsi biaya $C(\\theta) := \\langle "
"\\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle$ dapat dinyatakan sebagai"
" deret Fourier dengan cara berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& := \\langle \\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& := \\langle \\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "& := a_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)] \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& := a_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)] \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Depending on the periodicity and bandwidth of the original function, the set"
" $S$ may be finite or infinite. For the purposes of this discussion, we will"
" assume it is infinite. The next step is to sample the cost function "
"$C(\\theta)$ multiple times in order to obtain the Fourier coefficients "
"$\\{a_0, a_k, b_k\\}_{k=1}^S$. Specifically, since we have $2S+1$ unknowns, "
"we will need to sample the cost function $2S+1$ times.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tergantung pada periodisitas dan bandwidth fungsi asli, himpunan $S$ bisa "
"terbatas atau tak terbatas. Untuk keperluan diskusi ini, kita akan "
"mengasumsikan ia tak terbatas. Langkah berikutnya adalah mensampel fungsi "
"biaya $C(\\theta)$ beberapa kali untuk mendapatkan koefisien Fourier "
"$\\{a_0, a_k, b_k\\}_{k=1}^S$. Secara khusus, karena kita memiliki $2S+1$ "
"unknown, kita perlu mensampel fungsi biaya sebanyak $2S+1$ kali.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we then sample the cost function for $2S+1$ parameter values "
"$\\{\\theta_1,...,\\theta_{2S+1}\\}$, we can obtain the following system:\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kita kemudian mensampel fungsi biaya untuk nilai parameter $2S+1$ yaitu"
" $\\{\\theta_1,...,\\theta_{2S+1}\\}$, kita dapat memperoleh sistem "
"berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & \\cos(\\theta_1) & \\sin(\\theta_1) & \\cos(2\\theta_1) & ... & \\sin(S\\theta_1) \\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_2) & \\sin(\\theta_2) & \\cos(2\\theta_2) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_2)\\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\sin(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cos(2\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_{2S+1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} a_0 \\\\ a_1 \\\\ b_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ b_S \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} C(\\theta_1) \\\\ C(\\theta_2) \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ C(\\theta_{2S+1}) \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & \\cos(\\theta_1) & \\sin(\\theta_1) & \\cos(2\\theta_1) & ... & \\sin(S\\theta_1) \\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_2) & \\sin(\\theta_2) & \\cos(2\\theta_2) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_2)\\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\sin(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cos(2\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_{2S+1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} a_0 \\\\ a_1 \\\\ b_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ b_S \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} C(\\theta_1) \\\\ C(\\theta_2) \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ C(\\theta_{2S+1}) \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "that we'll rewrite as\n"
msgstr "yang akan kita tulis ulang sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Fa=c.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Fa=c.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In practice, this system is generally not consistent because the cost "
"function values $c$ are not exact. Therefore, it is usually a good idea to "
"normalize them by multiplying them by $F^\\dagger$ on the left, which "
"results in:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam praktiknya, sistem ini umumnya tidak konsisten karena nilai fungsi "
"biaya $c$ tidak tepat. Oleh karena itu, biasanya ide yang baik untuk "
"menormalisasinya dengan mengalikannya dengan $F^\\dagger$ di sebelah kiri, "
"yang menghasilkan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"F^\\dagger Fa = F^\\dagger c.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"F^\\dagger Fa = F^\\dagger c.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This new system is always consistent, and its solution is a least-squares "
"solution to the original problem. If we have $k$ parameters instead of just "
"one, and each parameter $\\theta^i$ has its own $S_i$ for $i \\in "
"{1,...,k}$, then the total number of samples required is:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sistem baru ini selalu konsisten, dan solusinya adalah solusi least-squares "
"dari masalah asli. Jika kita memiliki $k$ parameter alih-alih hanya satu, "
"dan setiap parameter $\\theta^i$ memiliki $S_i$-nya sendiri untuk $i \\in "
"{1,...,k}$, maka jumlah total sampel yang diperlukan adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $S_{\\max} = \\max_i(S_i)$. Furthermore, adjusting $S_{\\max}$ as a "
"tunable parameter (instead of inferring it) opens up new possibilities, such"
" as:\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $S_{\\max} = \\max_i(S_i)$. Selain itu, menyesuaikan $S_{\\max}$ "
"sebagai parameter yang bisa diatur (alih-alih menyimpulkannya) membuka "
"kemungkinan baru, seperti:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Over-sampling** to improve accuracy.\n"
msgstr "**Over-sampling** untuk meningkatkan akurasi.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Under-sampling** to boost performance by reducing runtime overhead or "
"eliminating local minima.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Under-sampling** untuk meningkatkan performa dengan mengurangi overhead "
"runtime atau menghilangkan local minima.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout-3}"
msgstr "Tata letak teoritis {#theoretical-layout-3}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "QSR's layout can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr "Tata letak QSR dapat dirangkum sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare reference operators $U_R$.\n"
msgstr "Siapkan operator referensi $U_R$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We'll go from the state $|0\\rangle$ to the reference state $|\\rho\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "Kita akan pergi dari state $|0\\rangle$ ke state referensi $|\\rho\\rangle$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Apply the  variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to create an ansatz "
"$U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terapkan variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ untuk membuat ansatz "
"$U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Determine the bandwidth associated with each parameter in the ansatz. An "
"upper bound is sufficient.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tentukan bandwidth yang terkait dengan setiap parameter dalam ansatz. Batas "
"atas sudah cukup.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bootstrap at $i=0$ if we have a similar problem (typically found by "
"classical simulation or sampling).\n"
msgstr ""
"Bootstrap pada $i=0$ jika kita punya masalah serupa (biasanya ditemukan "
"dengan simulasi atau sampling klasik).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sample the cost function $C(\\vec\\theta) := a_0 + "
"\\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)]$ at least $T$ times.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sampel fungsi biaya $C(\\vec\\theta) := a_0 + "
"\\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)]$ minimal $T$ kali.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n$\n"
msgstr "$T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Decide whether to over-sample/under-sample to balance speed vs accuracy by "
"adjusting $T$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Putuskan apakah akan over-sampling/under-sampling untuk menyeimbangkan "
"kecepatan vs akurasi dengan menyesuaikan $T$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute the Fourier coefficients from the samples (that is, solve the "
"normalized linear system of equations).\n"
msgstr ""
"Hitung koefisien Fourier dari sampel (yaitu, selesaikan sistem persamaan "
"linear yang dinormalisasi).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Solve for the global minimum of the resulting regression function on a "
"classical machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selesaikan untuk minimum global dari fungsi regresi yang dihasilkan pada "
"mesin klasik.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#summary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this lesson, you learned about multiple variational instances "
"available:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan pelajaran ini, kamu telah belajar tentang beberapa instance "
"variasional yang tersedia:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "General layout\n"
msgstr "Tata letak umum\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Introducing weights and penalties to adjust a cost function\n"
msgstr "Memperkenalkan bobot dan penalti untuk menyesuaikan fungsi biaya\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Exploring under-sampling vs over-sampling to trade-off speed vs accuracy\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengeksplorasi under-sampling vs over-sampling untuk trade-off kecepatan vs "
"akurasi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These ideas can be adapted to form a custom variational algorithm that fits "
"your problem. We encourage you to share your results with the community. The"
" next lesson will explore how to use a variational algorithm to solve an "
"application.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ide-ide ini dapat diadaptasi untuk membentuk algoritma variasional kustom "
"yang sesuai dengan masalahmu. Kami mendorongmu untuk berbagi hasilmu dengan "
"komunitas. Pelajaran berikutnya akan mengeksplorasi cara menggunakan "
"algoritma variasional untuk menyelesaikan suatu aplikasi.\n"
